cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ExciFinder in research or professional work, please cite the software using the metadata below."
title: "ExciFinder"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ramírez-Saco"
    given-names: "David"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3869-9534"
version: "2.1.3"
date-released: 2026-10-08
repository-code: "https://github.com/RamSacDavid/ExciFinder"
url: "https://qshhfj-d0ram0rez.shinyapps.io/ExciFinder/"
license: "AGPL-3.0-only"
abstract: >-
  ExciFinder is an open-source R/Shiny application for deterministic and
  traceable retrieval, organization, and verification of official information
  on excipients in medicinal products authorized and marketed in Spain. It
  queries CIMA/AEMPS sources, preserves source provenance, and reports factual
  conclusions separately from verification coverage.
keywords:
  - excipients
  - clinical pharmacology
  - drug information
  - medication safety
  - regulatory science
  - CIMA
  - AEMPS
  - R
  - Shiny
  - open science
